1. Delta Changes (diff, lag): Capture abrupt changes in e, v, or loc between adjacent modules, potentially exposing defect-prone transitions.
2. Comment and Blank Densities (derived from ratio): Indicates documentation quality and structural organization.

By leveraging these methods, both raw features and derived metrics provide clearer insights into maintainability, complexity, and defect-prone areas, improving prediction robustness.
